### ============================================
### AUTHENTICATION ENDPOINTS
### ============================================
### Base URL: http://localhost:29000/api/v1/auth
### All endpoints require proper headers and request bodies

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:29000
@authPath = /api/v1/auth

### Token Variables (set automatically after signin, or set manually)
@accessToken = 
@refreshToken = 
@userId =

### ============================================
### SIGNUP FLOW
### ============================================

### 1. Send SMS Verification Code for Signup
### Rate Limit: 3 requests/hour per IP
POST {{baseUrl}}{{authPath}}/signup/send-sms
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Id: device-12345
X-Forwarded-For: 192.168.1.1

{
  "phoneNumber": "+79147116738"
}

### 2. Verify SMS Code and Get Signup Token
POST {{baseUrl}}{{authPath}}/signup/verify-sms
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Id: device-12345
X-Forwarded-For: 192.168.1.1

{
  "phoneNumber": "+79147116738",
  "smsCode": "8481"
}

### 3. Complete User Signup with Signup Token (without referral code)
POST {{baseUrl}}{{authPath}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Id: device-12345
X-Forwarded-For: 192.168.1.1

{
  "signUpToken": "***REMOVED***",
  "phoneNumber": "+79147116735",
  "email": "kairosstroud1205@gmail.com",
  "password": "***REMOVED***",
  "username": "Kairos",
  "firstName": "Stroud",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "country": "USA",
  "city": "New York",
  "telegramId": "@johndoe"
}

### 4. Complete User Signup with Signup Token (WITH referral code)
### This will automatically create a referral relationship
POST {{baseUrl}}{{authPath}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Id: device-12345
X-Forwarded-For: 192.168.1.1

{
  "signUpToken": "***REMOVED***",
  "phoneNumber": "+79147116738",
  "email": "devboostx@gmail.com",
  "password": "***REMOVED***",
  "username": "stroud",
  "firstName": "Stroud",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "country": "USA",
  "city": "Los Angeles",
  "telegramId": "@hinokami",
  "referralCode": "0D14A7A2"
}

### ============================================
### EMAIL VERIFICATION FLOW
### ============================================

### 1. Send Email Verification Code
### Rate Limit: 3 requests/hour per email
POST {{baseUrl}}{{authPath}}/email/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com"
}

### 2. Verify Email Code
POST {{baseUrl}}{{authPath}}/email/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "code": "1234"
}

### ============================================
### PROFILE EMAIL VERIFICATION (AUTHENTICATED)
### ============================================

### 1. Send Email Verification Code to Profile
### Rate Limit: 3 requests/hour
### Requires: Authentication (Bearer token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me/email/send
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 2. Verify Email Code for Profile
### Requires: Authentication (Bearer token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me/email/verify
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "code": "1234"
}

### ============================================
### SIGNIN
### ============================================

### Sign In with Phone and Password
POST {{baseUrl}}{{authPath}}/signin
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Id: device-12345
X-Forwarded-For: 192.168.1.1

{
  "phoneNumber": "+79147116738",
  "password": "***REMOVED***"
}

> {%
    // Save tokens for use in other requests
    if (response.status === 200 && response.body.data) {
        client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.data.accessToken);
        client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.data.refreshToken);
        client.global.set("userId", response.body.data.userId);
    }
%}

### ============================================
### TOKEN MANAGEMENT
### ============================================

### Refresh Access Token
POST {{baseUrl}}{{authPath}}/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

> {%
    if (response.status === 200 && response.body.data) {
        client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.data.accessToken);
        client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.data.refreshToken);
    }
%}

### Sign Out (Invalidate Tokens)
### Note: Run the signin request first to set accessToken and userId variables
### The signout endpoint only requires the Authorization header, no request body needed
POST {{baseUrl}}{{authPath}}/signout
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-User-Id: {{userId}}

